  title: Gurjara-Pratiharas
  text: The Gurjara-Pratiharas ruled western and northern India from the 8th to the 10th centuries, eventually from Kannauj. Rulers such as Nagabhata the First and Mihira Bhoja resisted Arab expansion from Sindh.
